/T (Text2)
/Type /Annot
/V (Rahul Gupta meets the requirements for this award because his contributions combine deployed industrial innovation with unusually broad academic influence\056 From an academic perspective\054 what distinguishes Rahul is that he has not treated Responsible AI as only an internal product function\056 He has helped turn industrial safety problems into research agendas\054 shared tasks\054 workshops\054 and university collaborations that the research community can study\054 reproduce\054 and extend\056 His technical work includes BOLD for bias measurement\054 FLIRT for feedback\055loop red\055teaming\054 fairness methods for large\055scale natural language understanding systems\054 and CBRN uplift evaluation for frontier language models\056 These are not isolated papers\073 they form part of a larger program for measuring\054 evaluating\054 and improving trustworthy AI systems at scale\056 Rahul has helped organize TrustNLP\054 Trustworthy Speech Processing\054 the SemEval Unlearning Challenge\054 and the Nova Trusted AI Challenge\054 which drew more than 100 applications and engaged 10 university teams\056 He has also helped connect Amazon Academic Research Award collaborations representing more than \04420M in funded academic research to Responsible AI topics\056 His publication record\054 close to 5\054000 citations\054 and 25\053 patented or patent\055pending technologies show both research uptake and translation into practice\056 In my judgment\054 Rahul\047s achievement stands out because it created a durable bridge between frontier industrial AI systems and the academic ecosystem needed to evaluate and improve them\056)
/AP <<
/N 204 0 R
>>
>>
endobj
