/Helv 12.0 Tf 0 g
2 142.41600000000003 Td
(I know Rahul through the Responsible AI research community and his academic ecosystem-building around trustworthy language and speech processing. I became aware of his contributions through his publications, workshop leadership, academic challenges, and programs connecting industry-scale AI safety problems with universities. His work on TrustNLP, trustworthy speech processing venues, SemEval Unlearning, and the Nova Trusted AI Challenge is unusually visible to academic researchers working on reliable AI systems.) Tj
ET
Q
EMC
Q

endstream
endobj
204 0 obj
<<
/Type /XObject
/Subtype /Form
/BBox [ 0.0 0.0 507.1558 455.427 ]
/Length 1653
/Resources <<
/Font <<
/Helv 4 0 R
>>
>>
>>
stream
q
/Tx BMC 
q
2 1 503.1558 453.42699999999996 re
W
BT
/Helv 12.0 Tf 0 g
2 445.25499999999994 Td
(Rahul Gupta meets the requirements for this award because his contributions combine deployed industrial innovation with unusually broad academic influence. From an academic perspective, what distinguishes Rahul is that he has not treated Responsible AI as only an internal product function. He has helped turn industrial safety problems into research agendas, shared tasks, workshops, and university collaborations that the research community can study, reproduce, and extend. His technical work includes BOLD for bias measurement, FLIRT for feedback-loop red-teaming, fairness methods for large-scale natural language understanding systems, and CBRN uplift evaluation for frontier language models. These are not isolated papers; they form part of a larger program for measuring, evaluating, and improving trustworthy AI systems at scale. Rahul has helped organize TrustNLP, Trustworthy Speech Processing, the SemEval Unlearning Challenge, and the Nova Trusted AI Challenge, which drew more than 100 applications and engaged 10 university teams. He has also helped connect Amazon Academic Research Award collaborations representing more than $20M in funded academic research to Responsible AI topics. His publication record, close to 5,000 citations, and 25+ patented or patent-pending technologies show both research uptake and translation into practice. In my judgment, Rahul's achievement stands out because it created a durable bridge between frontier industrial AI systems and the academic ecosystem needed to evaluate and improve them.) Tj
ET
Q
EMC
Q

endstream
endobj
